[Bosco] THIS IS VERONA WESTLAKE.
THIS IS MIA'S SISTER.

118
00:06:31,434 --> 00:06:33,393
YOU MUST BE CBI, TOO?

119
00:06:33,393 --> 00:06:35,569
I'M AGENT LISBON.
THAT'S PATRICK JANE.

120
00:06:35,569 --> 00:06:37,266
HI.

121
00:06:37,266 --> 00:06:39,355
UH, MY HUSBAND DUNCAN WEAVER.HEY.

122
00:06:39,355 --> 00:06:41,183
MORE CBI?

123
00:06:41,183 --> 00:06:43,403
WHERE DID YOU GUYS COME FROM,
ANYWAY?

124
00:06:43,403 --> 00:06:47,711
TWO DAYS AGO,
I NEVER HEARD OF YOU.YOU NEITHER. NICE PLACE.

125
00:06:47,711 --> 00:06:50,322
YOU GUYS MUST BE LOADED.
HOW DID YOU MAKE THE MONEY?

126
00:06:50,322 --> 00:06:53,369
UH, MY GRANDFATHER, ACTUALLY--
OIL, LUMBER.

127
00:06:53,369 --> 00:06:55,371
OH! I JUST ASSUMED
IT WAS NEW MONEY,

128
00:06:55,371 --> 00:06:59,593
BECAUSE OF THE, UH,
THE DECOR.

129
00:06:59,593 --> 00:07:03,335
[lowers voice] UM, ALREADY
YOU START WITH THIS CRAP?

130
00:07:03,335 --> 00:07:05,425
[lowers voice] WHAT? WHAT?

131
00:07:05,425 --> 00:07:07,775
UH, BELINDA SANDBORNE,
VERONA'S ATTORNEY.

132
00:07:07,775 --> 00:07:10,691
ANY CONVERSATION YOU HAVE
WITH VERONA OR DUNCAN,

133
00:07:10,691 --> 00:07:14,434
I NEED TO BE THERE.NOT A PROBLEM. IS THERE
SOMEONE ELSE IN THE FAMILY

134
00:07:14,434 --> 00:07:17,219
WE SHOULD BE TALKING TO?

135
00:07:17,219 --> 00:07:20,396
I'M SORT OF... THE FAMILY.

136
00:07:20,396 --> 00:07:22,311
OUR PARENTS ARE DEAD.

137
00:07:22,311 --> 00:07:24,574
[sniffles]

138
00:07:24,574 --> 00:07:28,883
YOU KNOW, MIA--
SHE'S THE GROWN-UP, CAPABLE ONE.

139
00:07:28,883 --> 00:07:30,885
I'M THE MESS.

140
00:07:30,885 --> 00:07:32,800
HEY.

141
00:07:32,800 --> 00:07:35,367
TOO BAD, HUH?
THEY TOOK THE WRONG SISTER.

142
00:07:35,367 --> 00:07:36,804
YOU'RE DOING FINE.

143
00:07:36,804 --> 00:07:39,067
LISTEN TO THE MAN
WITH THE GUN, BABE.

144
00:07:39,067 --> 00:07:42,418
WE UNDERSTAND YOU'RE
INVESTIGATING A RELATED CASE?

145
00:07:42,418 --> 00:07:44,594
ANOTHER KIDNAPPING
THAT MAY HAVE BEEN CARRIED OUT

146
00:07:44,594 --> 00:07:48,337
BY THE SAME PEOPLE, YES.HOW DID IT, UM, TURN OUT?

147
00:07:48,337 --> 00:07:51,819
DID THE--DID THE PERSON
THEY TOOK GET HOME OKAY?

148
00:07:51,819 --> 00:07:54,299
NO. HE WAS KILLED.

149
00:07:57,085 --> 00:08:00,871
HIS NAME IS COLIN HAYMER.
HERE'S HIS PICTURE.

150
00:08:00,871 --> 00:08:04,396
HE'S FROM PACIFIC HEIGHTS.
DOES HE LOOK FAMILIAR?

151
00:08:04,396 --> 00:08:06,703
NO. YOU, BABE?

152
00:08:06,703 --> 00:08:08,662
NOTHING. SORRY.

153
00:08:08,662 --> 00:08:11,708
DOES HIS NAME EVER COME UP
IN ANY CONTEXT, EVEN CASUALLY?

154
00:08:11,708 --> 00:08:13,797
I DON'T THINK SO.

155
00:08:13,797 --> 00:08:16,234
HE WAS WORKING AT A COMPANY
CALLED STRAF INVESTMENTS

156
00:08:16,234 --> 00:08:19,107
WHEN HE WAS TAKEN. DO YOU HAVE
ANYTHING TO DO WITH THEM?

157
00:08:19,107 --> 00:08:21,239
STRAF?

158
00:08:21,239 --> 00:08:23,328
UM... BELINDA?

159
00:08:23,328 --> 00:08:26,288
NO, I DON'T THINK SO.
I'LL CHECK THE RECORDS.

160
00:08:26,288 --> 00:08:28,725
I'M SORRY I'M NOT REALLY
HELPING. I'M TRYING.

161
00:08:28,725 --> 00:08:30,727
I'M--I'M NOT...

162
00:08:30,727 --> 00:08:34,644
HELLO! OKAY. [chuckles]

163
00:08:34,644 --> 00:08:37,517
LOOK WHAT I FOUND.OH, GOD.

164
00:08:37,517 --> 00:08:39,083
UH, LEVI,
WHAT ARE YOU DOING IN HERE?

165
00:08:39,083 --> 00:08:41,390
SHE'S YOURS?

166
00:08:41,390 --> 00:08:45,002
YES. UH, MRS. KENT?
WHERE IS SHE?MRS. KENT!

167
00:08:45,002 --> 00:08:48,005
OH, SHE'S FINE. UM...
[sniffs] SHE'S A LITTLE SMELLY,

168
00:08:48,005 --> 00:08:50,704
BUT, UH, OTHER THAN THAT,
SHE'S A LITTLE CHERUB.

169
00:08:50,704 --> 00:08:52,270
SORRY, SORRY.

170
00:08:52,270 --> 00:08:54,403
MRS. KENT,
PLEASE KEEP HER IN HER ROOM.

171
00:08:54,403 --> 00:08:57,319
WE DISCUSSED THIS.YES, MA'AM.

172
00:08:57,319 --> 00:08:59,539
BOSS, RANSOM DEMAND
JUST CAME IN.

173
00:08:59,539 --> 00:09:01,062
COME ON.

174
00:09:01,062 --> 00:09:03,194
EXCUSE ME.SORRY.

175
00:09:07,198 --> 00:09:09,070
[makes popping sound]

176
00:09:12,464 --> 00:09:15,642
AH.

177
00:09:15,642 --> 00:09:18,862
IT'S A VIDEO ATTACHMENT
TO AN E-MAIL.

178
00:09:18,862 --> 00:09:22,257
CAN YOU GET THE I.P. ADDRESS?OH, I'M TRYING,

179
00:09:22,257 --> 00:09:25,042
BUT THEY ROUTED IT
THROUGH A BUNCH OF SERVERS.

180
00:09:25,042 --> 00:09:26,783
IT MIGHT TAKE DAYS. [speaks indistinctly]

181
00:09:26,783 --> 00:09:28,829
[gasps]

182
00:09:28,829 --> 00:09:31,222
YOU--YOU WANT ME
TO READ THIS?

183
00:09:33,442 --> 00:09:36,184
OKAY.

184
00:09:39,970 --> 00:09:44,366
"MY NAME IS MIA WESTLAKE.
I AM NOT HURT.

185
00:09:44,366 --> 00:09:46,411
"I AM BEING TREATED WELL.

186
00:09:46,411 --> 00:09:49,501
"FOR MY SAFE RETURN,

187
00:09:49,501 --> 00:09:53,767
"YOU MUST PAY $3.75 MILLION

188
00:09:53,767 --> 00:09:56,421
"IN SMALL, NONSEQUENTIAL BILLS.

189
00:09:56,421 --> 00:10:00,687
"THIS MONEY IS TO BE READY
BY 6:00 P.M. TONIGHT.

190
00:10:00,687 --> 00:10:04,255
"YOU WILL BE INSTRUCTED
WHAT TO DO THEN.

191
00:10:04,255 --> 00:10:06,736
FAILURE TO COMPLY
WILL RESULT..."

192
00:10:10,697 --> 00:10:13,177
"IN MY IMMEDIATE EXECUTION."

193
00:10:13,177 --> 00:10:15,223
[crying]

194
00:10:15,223 --> 00:10:18,530
"ANY INTERFERENCE WILL RESULT
IN MY IMMEDIATE EXECUTION."

195
00:10:18,530 --> 00:10:20,228
VERONA, IF YOU'RE
WATCHING THIS, I...

196
00:10:23,274 --> 00:10:25,973
DID YOU SEE THE TAT
ON THAT GUY?YEAH.

197
00:10:25,973 --> 00:10:29,367
I MEAN, THAT LOOKS
LIKE MEXICAN MAFIA.MM.

198
00:10:29,367 --> 00:10:31,892
WE'RE NOT GONNA GET ANYTHING
OUT OF THE WESTLAKES NOW.

199
00:10:31,892 --> 00:10:33,589
LET'S GO.

200
00:10:33,589 --> 00:10:37,419
$3.75 MILLION--VERY SPECIFIC
NUMBER, DON'T YOU THINK?

201
00:10:37,419 --> 00:10:39,421
MAYBE THE KIDNAPPERS
HAVE THEIR EYE

202
00:10:39,421 --> 00:10:41,205
ON THE WESTLAKES' BANK ACCOUNT.

203
00:10:41,205 --> 00:10:43,730
I'LL TALK TO BOSCO ABOUT IT,
THEN WE'LL GO.

204
00:10:43,730 --> 00:10:45,732
OKAY. TAKE YOUR TIME.

205
00:10:51,868 --> 00:10:55,655
WH--HEY, EXCUSE ME.
UH, WE'D LIKE SOME PRIVACY.

206
00:10:55,655 --> 00:10:58,832
I CAN UNDERSTAND THAT.
WHAT'S IN YOUR POCKET?

207
00:10:58,832 --> 00:11:01,530
NONE OF YOUR BUSINESS.

208
00:11:01,530 --> 00:11:03,488
YOU JUST KEEP TAPPING IT...

209
00:11:03,488 --> 00:11:05,534
TAP, TAP, TAPPING IT.

210
00:11:05,534 --> 00:11:09,581
WHATEVER IS IN THERE, YOU'RE
OBVIOUSLY NERVOUS ABOUT IT.

211
00:11:09,581 --> 00:11:13,411
I'M ASSUMING IT'S ILLEGAL.[pouring liquid]

212
00:11:13,411 --> 00:11:16,458
MY BEST GUESS WOULD BE...
DRUGS.

213
00:11:16,458 --> 00:11:18,895
UH, DO--DO YOU HAVE
ANY LEMON?

214
00:11:18,895 --> 00:11:21,202
I'M GONNA GO FIND
YOUR BOSS, ALL RIGHT?

215
00:11:21,202 --> 00:11:23,334
OKAY. WELL, BE SURE
TO TELL HER ABOUT THE DRUGS

216
00:11:23,334 --> 00:11:26,163
IN YOUR TOP POCKET.
IF YOU NEED ME,

217
00:11:26,163 --> 00:11:28,339
I'M GONNA BE RIGHT HERE
TALKING TO YOUR LOVELY WIFE.

218
00:11:28,339 --> 00:11:30,472
[voice breaking]
PLEASE LEAVE, ALL RIGHT?

219
00:11:30,472 --> 00:11:33,475
I JUST WANT TO BE ALONE.THAT'S WHAT WE ALL WANT.
NO ONE GETS IT.

220
00:11:33,475 --> 00:11:35,085
SO THERE'S NO LEMONS HERE?

221
00:11:35,085 --> 00:11:37,087
NO, I DON'T THINK SO!

222
00:11:37,087 --> 00:11:40,090
I REALLY FELT LIKE...
MM, NEVER MIND.

223
00:11:40,090 --> 00:11:42,658
YOUR SISTER
NEEDS YOU HERE NOW.

224
00:11:42,658 --> 00:11:46,357
AS COMFORTING AS IT MIGHT BE
TO CRAWL UNDER THE BLANKET

225
00:11:46,357 --> 00:11:50,535
OF NARCOTICS THAT YOUR HUSBAND
HAS SO GENEROUSLY PROCURED

226
00:11:50,535 --> 00:11:53,147
FOR YOU,
IT'S BETTER THAT YOU DON'T.

227
00:11:53,147 --> 00:11:55,540
[sniffles] NOTHING I DO
IS GOING TO HELP HER.

228
00:11:55,540 --> 00:11:58,021
YOU'RE PROBABLY RIGHT.

229
00:11:58,021 --> 00:11:59,631
WHAT'S THE POINT?

230
00:11:59,631 --> 00:12:03,374
WHAT YOU CAN ACCOMPLISH
IS IRRELEVANT.

231
00:12:03,374 --> 00:12:06,421
BUT IF YOU ARE ABSENT
IN THIS MOMENT,

232
00:12:06,421 --> 00:12:08,423
YOU WILL REGRET IT
FOR THE REST

233
00:12:08,423 --> 00:12:11,208
OF WHAT WILL BE
A MISERABLE LIFE.

234
00:12:13,471 --> 00:12:16,257
THAT'S ALL.

235
00:12:16,257 --> 00:12:17,824
SEE YOU.

236
00:12:26,397 --> 00:12:28,748
[Lisbon] WHAT WERE YOU
DOING BACK THERE?

237
00:12:28,748 --> 00:12:31,446
OH, JUST GETTING A SNACK,
A LITTLE LIGHT REFRESHMENT.

238
00:12:31,446 --> 00:12:35,276
WHY DON'T I BELIEVE YOU?WHAT? W-WHAT IS THIS?

239
00:12:35,276 --> 00:12:38,888
THIS IS PROOF OF MY VERACITY.IT'S TIME TO GO.

240
00:12:38,888 --> 00:12:42,457
I'M GONNA STAY.I KNOW WHAT THIS IS ABOUT.
BOSCO'S GOT THE RED JOHN FILE.

241
00:12:42,457 --> 00:12:45,286
YOU THINK IF YOU HANG AROUND
LONG ENOUGH,

242
00:12:45,286 --> 00:12:48,376
YOU'LL WEASEL YOUR WAY INTO IT."WEASEL" IS A LITTLE STRONG.

243
00:12:48,376 --> 00:12:50,465
YOU'RE WASTING YOUR TIME.
BOSCO WILL NEVER GO FOR IT.

244
00:12:50,465 --> 00:12:52,336
NEVER.

245
00:12:52,336 --> 00:12:55,600
WHAT?
I'LL NEVER GO FOR WHAT?I LIKE THE WAY YOU WORK.

246
00:12:55,600 --> 00:12:58,386
I WANT TO WORK ON YOUR TEAM
ON THE, UH, KIDNAPPING DETAIL.

247
00:12:58,386 --> 00:13:00,562
OH, YOU DO, HUH?

248
00:13:00,562 --> 00:13:02,390
A LIVE KIDNAPPING VICTIM
IS SO MUCH MORE MY SPEED

249
00:13:02,390 --> 00:13:05,393
THAN A SHRIVELED CORPSE.LIKE I CARE ABOUT YOUR SPEED.

250
00:13:05,393 --> 00:13:08,788
LISBON, YOU CLAIM TO HAVE
CONTROL OVER THIS WHACK-JOB.

251
00:13:08,788 --> 00:13:12,313
WHY DON'T YOU DO ME A FAVOR
AND WALK HIM AWAY?DON'T TALK TO ME THAT WAY.

252
00:13:12,313 --> 00:13:15,577
YEAH, THAT'S VERY RUDE.QUIET. MINELLI GAVE US
SPECIFIC ORDERS.

253
00:13:15,577 --> 00:13:19,363
I DON'T GIVE A FLYING--HEY. HEY, HEY, HEY!
YOU THIS AGENT'S BOSS?

254
00:13:19,363 --> 00:13:22,584
WHY?I WANT HIM REMOVED
FROM THIS CASE NOW.

255
00:13:22,584 --> 00:13:24,716
NOW,ALL RIGHT?

256
00:13:24,716 --> 00:13:27,676
HE'S--HE'S DISRESPECTFUL
AND, UH, RUDE

257
00:13:27,676 --> 00:13:30,374
AND--AND UNPROFESSIONAL.OH, HE'S JUST ANGRY
'CAUSE I CALLED HIM

258
00:13:30,374 --> 00:13:34,726
ON HIS LITTLE DRUG DEAL THING.OKAY, YOU'RE NUTS.
I HAVE NO DRUGS.

259
00:13:34,726 --> 00:13:36,163
LIAR.

260
00:13:36,163 --> 00:13:38,600
I DEMAND YOU TAKE
THIS MAN OFF THE CASE,

261
00:13:38,600 --> 00:13:41,951
OR THERE WILL BE
SERIOUS CONSEQUENCES.WELL, SIR,
THAT'S NOT YOUR CALL.

262
00:13:41,951 --> 00:13:43,997
OH, YEAH? YOU THINK?

263
00:13:43,997 --> 00:13:46,869
ONE PHONE CALL, I CAN HAVE YOU
DIRECTING TRAFFIC.

264
00:13:46,869 --> 00:13:48,349
IS THAT RIGHT?

265
00:13:48,349 --> 00:13:50,394
YEAH, IT IS.

266
00:13:50,394 --> 00:13:53,397
WELL, MAKE YOUR CALL, BECAUSE
THIS MAN'S STAYING ON THE CASE

267
00:13:53,397 --> 00:13:56,357
WHETHER YOU LIKE IT OR NOT.REALLY?

268
00:13:56,357 --> 00:13:59,534
YEAH.YOU SEE--SEE THIS? YOU SEE
WHAT HE'S DONE TO MY WIFE?

269
00:13:59,534 --> 00:14:02,102
I MEAN,
THIS GUY'S OUT OF CONTROL.SHUT UP, DUNCAN.

270
00:14:02,102 --> 00:14:05,932
BABY,
I WAS TRYING TO EXPLAIN--SHUT UP.

271
00:14:05,932 --> 00:14:07,759
MR. JANE, IS IT?

272
00:14:07,759 --> 00:14:09,283
YEAH.

273
00:14:09,283 --> 00:14:14,679
WHAT YOU SAID EARLIER
WAS RIGHT. THANK YOU...

274
00:14:14,679 --> 00:14:16,507
I GUESS. [chuckles]

275
00:14:16,507 --> 00:14:19,380
[sniffles]
LEAVE HIM ALONE.

276
00:14:25,516 --> 00:14:27,910
OKAY, THEN. IT'S SETTLED.
HAVE FUN. BOYS.

277
00:14:34,525 --> 00:14:37,137
WAIT.

278
00:14:43,099 --> 00:14:45,145
FROM THE COLIN HAYMER CASE.

279
00:14:45,145 --> 00:14:48,104
SO YOU WANT NAMES THAT BEGIN
WITH "A" THROUGH "L"

280
00:14:48,104 --> 00:14:49,671
OR "M" THROUGH "Z"?"A" THROUGH "L."

281
00:14:49,671 --> 00:14:51,455
YOU GOT IT.

282
00:14:51,455 --> 00:14:53,631
CHANGED MY MIND.
I WANT "M" THROUGH "Z."

283
00:14:53,631 --> 00:14:55,285
TOO LATE. YOU ALREADY CHOSE.

284
00:14:55,285 --> 00:14:58,506
OH, COME ON.
ROCK, PAPER, SCISSORS? STEP UP.

285
00:14:58,506 --> 00:15:00,900
HEY, BERT, CAN I GET
ON THIS ROCK, PAPER, SCISSORS?

286
00:15:00,900 --> 00:15:03,554
I HAVEN'T HAD A REALLY GOOD
GAME SINCE I WAS, OH, 10.

287
00:15:03,554 --> 00:15:06,383
IT'S RIGSBY.

288
00:15:06,383 --> 00:15:08,777
I KNOW.

289
00:15:08,777 --> 00:15:11,954
HEY, WHAT'S WITH HICKS
CALLING ME BERT?

290
00:15:11,954 --> 00:15:14,609
UM, I'M SURE I DON'T KNOW.

291
00:15:14,609 --> 00:15:16,741
IT'S BERT, LIKE THE MUPPET.

292
00:15:16,741 --> 00:15:20,136
IT'S JUST A STUPID NICKNAME.
IT DOESN'T MEAN ANYTHING.

293
00:15:20,136 --> 00:15:22,138
BOSCO'S TEAM CALLS US
BERT AND ERNIE.

294
00:15:22,138 --> 00:15:24,793
YOU KNEW THAT,
AND YOU DIDN'T SAY ANYTHING?IT WOULD BOTHER YOU.

295
00:15:24,793 --> 00:15:26,969
IT DOESN'T BOTHER YOU?NO.

296
00:15:26,969 --> 00:15:29,885
WHY NOT?ERNIE'S THE CLEVER,
HANDSOME ONE.

297
00:15:29,885 --> 00:15:31,800
WHERE'S JANE?WITH BOSCO.

298
00:15:31,800 --> 00:15:34,194
DON'T ASK ME WHAT THEY'RE DOING,
BECAUSE I DON'T KNOW

299
00:15:34,194 --> 00:15:37,893
AND I DON'T CARE.
WHAT DO YOU GOT?I'VE BEEN CHECKING OUT
THE HOUSE

300
00:15:37,893 --> 00:15:40,635
WHERE WE FOUND
COLIN HAYMER'S BODY.

301
00:15:40,635 --> 00:15:42,550
IT'S BEEN ABANDONED
SEVEN YEARS.

302
00:15:42,550 --> 00:15:44,552
THERE WERE SOME COMPLAINTS
ABOUT SQUATTERS

303
00:15:44,552 --> 00:15:46,554
FIVE, SIX YEARS AGO.
NOTHING ELSE.

304
00:15:46,554 --> 00:15:49,470
AGENT LISBON,
THERE'S A LOUIS EARLEN

305
00:15:49,470 --> 00:15:52,473
TO SEE YOU IN YOUR OFFICE.KEEP DIGGING.

306
00:15:52,473 --> 00:15:53,648
RIGHT.

307
00:15:53,648 --> 00:15:55,606
LIEUTENANT EARLEN.

308
00:15:55,606 --> 00:15:58,348
THANKS FOR COMING.LOUIS, PLEASE. I'M RETIRED.

309
00:15:58,348 --> 00:16:01,177
SO YOU FOUND
POOR COLIN HAYMER?

310
00:16:01,177 --> 00:16:02,744
WE DID.

311
00:16:02,744 --> 00:16:04,920
YOU WERE THE S.F.P.D. OFFICER

312
00:16:04,920 --> 00:16:06,487
IN CHARGE OF THE KIDNAPPING
INVESTIGATION, RIGHT?

313
00:16:06,487 --> 00:16:10,230
I WAS. SPENT A LOT OF TIME
WITH THE HAYMER FAMILY.

314
00:16:10,230 --> 00:16:12,623
HAVE THEY BEEN NOTIFIED?THEY HAVE.

315
00:16:12,623 --> 00:16:14,625
OH. HOPE IT'S SOME KIND
OF CONSOLATION.

316
00:16:14,625 --> 00:16:16,845
THEY'VE BEEN WAITING
A LONG TIME FOR THAT BOY.

317
00:16:16,845 --> 00:16:18,890
WE HAVE ANOTHER KIDNAPPING.

318
00:16:18,890 --> 00:16:21,284
WE THINK THE SAME PEOPLE
MIGHT BE BEHIND IT.

319
00:16:21,284 --> 00:16:22,677
HOW CAN I HELP?

320
00:16:22,677 --> 00:16:24,679
ANYBODY YOU THINK
WE SHOULD TAKE A LOOK AT?

321
00:16:24,679 --> 00:16:27,464
[chuckles] TALL ORDER.
WE LOOKED AT A LOT OF PEOPLE.

322
00:16:27,464 --> 00:16:30,293
WELL, WE WERE WONDERING
IF MAYBE IT WAS AN INSIDE JOB.

323
00:16:30,293 --> 00:16:32,774
THE RANSOM DEMAND
WAS PRETTY SPECIFIC.

324
00:16:32,774 --> 00:16:34,471
WE CONSIDERED THAT.

325
00:16:34,471 --> 00:16:37,518
I ALWAYS HAD A FEELING
ABOUT COLIN'S GIRLFRIEND--

326
00:16:37,518 --> 00:16:40,303
NOTHING SOLID, JUST A FEELING.DO YOU REMEMBER HER NAME?

327
00:16:40,303 --> 00:16:43,480
DIANE ZAR... ZARANSKI.

328
00:16:43,480 --> 00:16:45,178
YEAH.

329
00:16:45,178 --> 00:16:47,180
TALKED TO HER
A COUPLE OF TIMES.

330
00:16:47,180 --> 00:16:48,920
WHEN'S THE RANSOM DROP?

331
00:16:48,920 --> 00:16:51,401
TONIGHT, 6:00.UH-HUH.

332
00:16:51,401 --> 00:16:53,447
THE NIGHT COLIN'S RANSOM
GOT PAID,

333
00:16:53,447 --> 00:16:57,625
I SAT WITH HIS PARENTS
TILL MORNING

334
00:16:57,625 --> 00:17:00,628
JUST WAITIN' TO HEAR
HE WAS SAFE.

335
00:17:00,628 --> 00:17:03,022
DON'T THINK WE SAID
TEN WORDS.

336
00:17:06,634 --> 00:17:09,376
[sighs]

337
00:17:09,376 --> 00:17:13,510
IF IT IS THE SAME PEOPLE
THAT TOOK COLIN,

338
00:17:13,510 --> 00:17:15,991
YOU DO THIS GIRL'S FAMILY
A FAVOR.

339
00:17:15,991 --> 00:17:17,471
MONEY DROPS AT 6:00.

340
00:17:17,471 --> 00:17:20,387
AT 6:01, YOU TELL THEM
THEIR CHILD IS DEAD,

341
00:17:20,387 --> 00:17:23,216
GIVE 'EM A CHANCE
TO GET USED TO IT.

342
00:17:23,216 --> 00:17:25,479
IT WOULD BE A KINDNESS.

343
00:17:37,534 --> 00:17:40,146
BOSS, I MIGHT HAVE SOMETHING.WHAT?

344
00:17:40,146 --> 00:17:42,539
THOSE SQUATTERS IN THE HOUSE
WHERE WE FOUND HAYMER?

345
00:17:42,539 --> 00:17:45,107
THEY WERE DRUG DEALERS.
A DETECTIVE IN OAKLAND NARCOTICS

346
00:17:45,107 --> 00:17:47,457
SAID THEY'RE AN EXTENDED
FAMILY--EIGHT OR TEN PEOPLE.

347
00:17:47,457 --> 00:17:49,459
THEY GREW POT ON A FARM
CALLED CRAZY HILL

348
00:17:49,459 --> 00:17:52,158
IN GOODHUE COUNTY,
BROUGHT IT INTO OAKLAND

349
00:17:52,158 --> 00:17:54,856
AND SOLD IT OUT OF THE HOUSE.AND THIS HAS TO DO
WITH COLIN HAYMER HOW?

350
00:17:54,856 --> 00:17:56,858
APPARENTLY,
THEY ALSO SOLD DRUGS

351
00:17:56,858 --> 00:17:59,078
THAT THEY BOUGHT
FROM BORDER CARTELS,

352
00:17:59,078 --> 00:18:01,428
ANDTHEY PICKED UP SOME
OF THE CARTELS' HABITS

353
00:18:01,428 --> 00:18:03,517
LIKE KIDNAPPING FOR CASH.

354
00:18:03,517 --> 00:18:06,563
SO THEY WENT FROM DEALING POT
TO KIDNAPPING WEALTHY KIDS?

355
00:18:06,563 --> 00:18:09,610
LESS EFFORT, MORE PROFIT.DO YOU HAVE ANY NAMES?

356
00:18:09,610 --> 00:18:11,612
THEY'RE KNOWN AS
THE CRAZY HILL GANG.

357
00:18:11,612 --> 00:18:13,962
ONE OF THE RINGLEADERS
WAS NICKNAMED "DEEZER."

358
00:18:13,962 --> 00:18:16,007
NOBODY KNOWS HIS REAL NAME.

359
00:18:16,007 --> 00:18:17,487
APPARENTLY,
DEEZER'S BEEN HANGING AROUND

360
00:18:17,487 --> 00:18:20,099
AN APARTMENT BUILDING
IN WEST OAKLAND.

361
00:18:20,099 --> 00:18:23,580
BOSS WANTS US TO CHECK
THE BUILDING OUT.FORGOT MY EXTRA MAGS.
MEET YOU DOWNSTAIRS.

362
00:18:23,580 --> 00:18:25,582
[lowers voice] "EXTRA MAGS."
MM. BIG MAN.

363
00:18:25,582 --> 00:18:27,280
WHERE'S YOUR VEST?

364
00:18:27,280 --> 00:18:28,585
[normal voice]
DON'T NEED ONE.

365
00:18:28,585 --> 00:18:30,761
SURE YOU DO.WE'RE JUST CANVASSING.

366
00:18:30,761 --> 00:18:33,895
FOR PEOPLE CALLED
"THE CRAZY HILL GANG."

367
00:18:33,895 --> 00:18:35,940
YOU SHOULD WEAR A VEST.

368
00:18:35,940 --> 00:18:38,160
LOOK, IT'S HOT.
IT'S UNCOMFORTABLE.

369
00:18:38,160 --> 00:18:40,684
HICKS ISN'T WEARING ONE.

370
00:18:40,684 --> 00:18:44,819
[scoffs] WHAT, YOU'RE AFRAID
HE'LL MAKE FUN OF YOU?NO. NOT AT ALL.

371
00:18:44,819 --> 00:18:47,343
[elevator bell dings,
doors open]DON'T BE AN IDIOT.
PUT ON A VEST.

372
00:18:53,523 --> 00:18:56,483
FINE. GET SHOT.
SEE IF I CARE.

373
00:19:04,621 --> 00:19:07,755
[speaks indistinctly]
THERE YOU GO.

374
00:19:07,755 --> 00:19:09,583
ONE MORE?

375
00:19:09,583 --> 00:19:10,714
SHE LIKES YOU.

376
00:19:10,714 --> 00:19:12,325
SHE HAS GOOD TASTE.

377
00:19:12,325 --> 00:19:15,502
YOU'RE GOOD WITH CHILDREN.UNLIKE YOUR EMPLOYERS?

378
00:19:15,502 --> 00:19:18,461
I DON'T KNOW WHAT YOU MEAN.OH, COME ON.

379
00:19:18,461 --> 00:19:20,724
IT'S CLEAR TO SEE THEY'RE
SKITTISH ABOUT THE PARENTING.

380
00:19:20,724 --> 00:19:23,466
I WOULDN'T KNOW
ANYTHING ABOUT THAT.

381
00:19:23,466 --> 00:19:25,425
VERONA'S LOW SELF-ESTEEM
MAKES HER DOUBT

382
00:19:25,425 --> 00:19:27,557
SHE'LL EVER BE A REAL PARENT.

383
00:19:27,557 --> 00:19:30,125
AND BECAUSE DUNCAN
MARRIED HER FOR HER MONEY,

384
00:19:30,125 --> 00:19:32,780
HE SEES THE CHILD
AS A RIVAL,

385
00:19:32,780 --> 00:19:35,565
IN MORE THAN
THE USUAL FREUDIAN TERM.

386
00:19:35,565 --> 00:19:37,915
THEY'RE VERY CARING PEOPLE,
VERY LOVING,

387
00:19:37,915 --> 00:19:41,528
JUST NOT PARTICULARLY HANDS-ON,
IF YOU KNOW WHAT I MEAN.

388
00:19:41,528 --> 00:19:45,880
HOW'S DUNCAN'S RELATIONSHIP
WITH MIA?

389
00:19:45,880 --> 00:19:48,491
IT CAN BE DIFFICULT.

390
00:19:48,491 --> 00:19:50,537
WELL, IT MAKES SENSE.

391
00:19:50,537 --> 00:19:54,105
IF HE SEES HIS CHILD AS A RIVAL,
WHY NOT HIS SISTER-IN-LAW?

392
00:19:54,105 --> 00:19:57,805
I'VE HEARD ANGRY WORDS
BETWEEN THEM.

393
00:19:57,805 --> 00:20:01,069
I THINK MIA
DOESN'T TRUST HIM.

394
00:20:01,069 --> 00:20:04,290
BUT I SHOULDN'T SAY ANYTHING.

395
00:20:04,290 --> 00:20:06,292
NO.

396
00:20:06,292 --> 00:20:09,643
BUT YOU DID.

397
00:20:09,643 --> 00:20:11,862
JANE,
WE GOT AN ERRAND TO RUN.

398
00:20:11,862 --> 00:20:13,168
OKAY.

399
00:20:13,168 --> 00:20:15,344
ALL RIGHT.
[clears throat] GOTTA GO.

400
00:20:15,344 --> 00:20:18,913
GOTTA GO AND RUN AN ERRAND
WITH THE BIG, SERIOUS MAN.COME ON. LET'S GO.

401
00:20:18,913 --> 00:20:21,132
BYE.

402
00:20:30,838 --> 00:20:32,840
SO WHAT'S THE DEAL HERE?

403
00:20:32,840 --> 00:20:36,017
WELL, THE TATTOO
ON THE KIDNAPPER'S ARM

404
00:20:36,017 --> 00:20:40,021
SUGGESTS THE, UH, MEXICAN MAFIA
MIGHT BE INVOLVED.MM-HMM.

405
00:20:40,021 --> 00:20:43,459
THOSE GUYS--THEY'RE MEMBERS.
SO WE'RE GONNA GO TALK TO 'EM.

406
00:20:43,459 --> 00:20:46,593
THEY LOOK SCARY.THEY ARE SCARY.

407
00:20:46,593 --> 00:20:50,031
YOU CAN'T BECAUSE A FULL MEMBER
UNTIL YOU'VE KILLED SOMEONE.

408
00:20:53,164 --> 00:20:54,775
MAYBE I'LL JUST WAIT
IN THE CAR.

409
00:20:54,775 --> 00:20:57,212
NO. YOU'RE COMING WITH ME.
I NEED YOU FOR BACKUP.

410
00:21:02,739 --> 00:21:04,350
BACKUP?

411
00:21:06,787 --> 00:21:09,572
HEY, FELLAS.

412
00:21:09,572 --> 00:21:12,836
HI. HOLA. ¿QúE PASó?

413
00:21:12,836 --> 00:21:15,709
UM, LISTEN,

414
00:21:15,709 --> 00:21:18,712
I'M AGENT, UH, BOSCO
WITH THE CBI.

415
00:21:18,712 --> 00:21:21,062
AGENT JANE.HI.

416
00:21:21,062 --> 00:21:23,194
I WAS WONDERING
IF ANY OF YOU FELLAS

417
00:21:23,194 --> 00:21:25,240
HAVE SEEN YOUR MAN SNOOPY?

418
00:21:25,240 --> 00:21:27,764
WE NEED TO TALK TO HIM.
SNOOPY?

419
00:21:27,764 --> 00:21:29,679
SNOOP.

420
00:21:29,679 --> 00:21:32,334
WE'RE LOOKIN' FOR HIM.
WE'D LIKE TO TALK TO HIM.

421
00:21:32,334 --> 00:21:34,423
HEY, KEEP WALKIN', MAN.

422
00:21:34,423 --> 00:21:36,860
WHO ARE YOU?

423
00:21:36,860 --> 00:21:39,733
WHY ARE YOU BEING THAT WAY?
I ASKED YOU NICELY.

424
00:21:39,733 --> 00:21:42,649
I-I ASKED--THE NAME IS RAOUL,

425
00:21:42,649 --> 00:21:45,434
AND I AIN'T GOT NO WARRANTS,
SO BACK UP, FOOL.

426
00:21:45,434 --> 00:21:48,176
WELL, RAOUL, YOU AND ME
ARE GONNA HAVE TO GO HAVE

427
00:21:48,176 --> 00:21:52,006
A PRIVATE CHAT IN A MOMENT.NAH. I AIN'T DID NOTHING WRONG.

428
00:21:52,006 --> 00:21:55,923
DON'T MAKE IT DIFFICULT.

429
00:21:55,923 --> 00:21:58,665
TOUGH GUYS, HUH?

430
00:21:58,665 --> 00:22:00,580
DEPENDS ON WHAT YOU MEAN
BY "TOUGH."

431
00:22:00,580 --> 00:22:02,495
EMOTIONALLY RESILIENT?
YES.

432
00:22:02,495 --> 00:22:05,280
SO NOW YOU
GONNA PLAY ME, TOO?

433
